Isotope: the lock screen in the login screen's look.

What: re-lays out the locker's menu (App::menu in src/locker.rs) over the
whole output, as 0001 does for the login screen, instead of a two-column
card 866 px wide:
- top left, the Isotope mark and the "ISOTOPE" wordmark (greeter-mark.svg
  under a dark theme, greeter-mark-day.svg under a light one);
- top right, a strip with the keyboard layout chooser, the on-screen keyboard
  toggle, and the network and battery icons;
- top centre, the date and a large clock (about 8.5% of the screen width);
- centre, the user's picture in a circle (or their initial), their name, the
  pill-shaped password field with its show-password (eye) button, and the
  caps-lock, authenticating and error lines under it;
- bottom, suspend as a round glass button with its label, when logind is
  there.
The stock locker's actions are kept and no action is added: it has the
on-screen keyboard, the keyboard layout and suspend (its accessibility
button is commented out upstream), and no restart or shut down. The
subsurface now covers the output from its top left (it was 866 px wide,
32 px down) in the three places that size it (output created, output info
update, session locked); the window size of each subsurface is recorded so
the clock scales with the output. The password field is the blurred region
of the surface (Common::blur_rects), as the card was.

The background: since epoch-1.11.0 the locker draws nothing on its lock
surface and cosmic-bg shows the user's wallpaper under it
(cosmic-session-lock-layer-v1). The lock screen now sets Common's
`background_rule` to the login screen's rule (greeter::background, now
pub(crate)), so for Isotope's two desktop wallpapers it draws the soft copy,
isotope-desktop-{night,day}-blur.png, over the whole surface. For any other
picture, a colour, an output with no wallpaper, or a soft copy that cannot
be read, it draws only the scrim of the theme's background colour (45%), so
cosmic-bg's sharp picture shows under it, as the login screen's scrim does.
The soft copy is a world-readable file in the image, read as the user.

What moved: the pieces of the login screen that both screens use are now
functions in src/common.rs instead of local code in greeter.rs's App::menu
and view_window: glass, glass_class, glass_button, glass_action,
strip_button, brand (the mark and wordmark), date_time (the date and the
scaled clock), avatar, on_wallpaper_class (the text and icon colour over the
wallpaper), scrim, and pill_input. The login screen calls them and looks the
same; only where the code lives changes. 0001 is left as it is (it is
checked in a VM) and this patch applies after it.

Two fixes to the locker's own flow, found in a VM:
- Common::update_wallpapers finds a surface's output by Common::output_names
  first. The locker drops a surface's name when it unlocks, so a wallpaper
  change while unlocked (the day/night switch of `isotope wallpaper-follow`)
  found no name, and every later lock drew only the scrim over cosmic-bg's
  sharp picture.
- Common::focus_input_on_open, set by the locker: when the lock screen's
  subsurface opens, the caret goes to its password field, as on the login
  screen. Before, typed keys were lost until a click in the field.

The log line "isotope-lock-screen: ..." at start is the tag
test/look/check-look.sh greps for in the binary.

Why: Isotope's look (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-20-isotope-look-design.md):
the lock screen must look like the login screen and the desktop. sway, niri
(swaylock) and i3 (i3lock) are themed from the palette by tools/gen-theme.py;
COSMIC's lock screen is cosmic-greeter's locker, which no config can lay out.

Made against cosmic-greeter epoch-1.11.0 (80e8a104b75a) with
0001-isotope-centred-login.patch applied, and libcosmic 430f3d48a97d.

